title: Changelog
new-page: true
is-special: true

= Changelog

**Version 0.12**: the first card and the first congress. The Party Discussion card lets the Zentrale back one faction's theses. The Leipzig congress is played motion by motion: you choose which version the Zentrale tables, the factions vote by their convictions, and the result moves the line, the party's appeal and Moscow. The party now has districts, each held by a faction, which send the delegates, and a Zentrale whose seats decide how restless the minorities get. Who wins in the Kremlin now depends partly on the KPD's own path. The Moscow tab is regrouped into three blocks, Balance of Forces is now Forces with strength and militarisation for each formation, the Politics list shows each party's ideology, and Missions has a new layout with room for an image.

**Version 0.11**: back to a bare foundation. All events, cards and advisors are taken out (the advisor slots stay, empty), and so are the member count and the economy. The Party tab now holds the other parties as well: the SPD, Centre, DDP, DVP and DNVP always, any other party once it polls 5%. A new Missions tab shows what the leading faction wants. A new faction, the Minor currents, cannot lead but counts at congresses. The Executive card is empty for now, and the Provinces card shows eight states without decisions. Balance of Forces lists every paramilitary league in its colours, with strength in words only. In the Moscow tab, whom each Kremlin leader backs is in the hover card.

**Version 0.10**: the first playable months. The Leipzig congress, the Saxon government crisis and the Moscow compromise; eight Party Affairs cards. The Provinces card shows all eighteen states with their parliaments, decisions and elections; the Executive card holds the Zentrale's decisions, including when the next congress meets. Congresses come about once a year, and Moscow's demands can be refused. The party starts with two camps, and the Middle Group, the Ultra-Left and the Thälmann circle form through events. New Moscow and Balance of Forces tabs; hover cards for the cabinet, the President and the Chancellor. The advisors are back.

**Version 0.9**: Moscow reworked. The Comintern's plenums meet on a fixed calendar, set the line and give the KPD a directive; the next plenum praises or rebukes the leadership, and a second rebuke brings an Open Letter that replaces it at the next congress. Four Kremlin patrons (Zinoviev, Trotsky and Radek, Bukharin, Stalin) rise and fall with the succession struggle, and each faction rises or falls with its patron. Moscow's pressure is shown in advance: no more dice.

**Version 0.8**: cards, advisors, events and endings are taken out while the game is rebuilt; the government line and the President show party colours; hover cards for Zinoviev and Radek.

**Version 0.7**: the menu links sit centred at the top; a panel on the right, empty for now; Replace an advisor sits next to the deck and End the month is gone; Reichstag seats and group results in percent; a new opening text about what the party can do.

**Version 0.6**: advisors: three posts in the Zentrale, ten historical candidates, each post acting once every six months, and a card to replace them; one Party Affairs deck instead of three, with the old cards taken out while they are rewritten; an End the month card; a tighter main page with four cards to a row; larger hover cards that look the same everywhere.

**Version 0.5**: an admin panel for achievements, images and texts; achievements can be unlocked; a centred layout; hover cards for parties and factions; party colours that follow each party's leadership; the KPD's leadership changes only at party congresses.

**Version 0.4**: a new title screen with a changelog and achievements; the game starts straight away with a hand of four cards; the party leader's portrait sits above the decks; exact numbers can be turned on in the options.

**Version 0.3**: the sidebar has four tabs (Main, Party, Politics, Polls) and focuses on the Republic, the other parties and the revolution; advisor slots; hover boxes always fit on the screen.

**Version 0.2**: a standalone game. You play the whole KPD, and your decisions strengthen or anger its five factions. Party colours.

**Version 0.1**: the first prototype, January 1923 to April 1924.

- @backSpecialScene: Back.
